  "content": {
    "id": "p38-q17-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "Let $P(8,y)$ lie on $y=f(x)$. Find the new $x$-coordinate of $P$ on each of the following.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p38-q17-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=f\\left(\\frac{x}{2}-2\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$20$",
          "worked": "Write $y=f\\left(\\frac{x-4}{2}\\right)$. Replace $x\\mapsto\\frac{x}{2}$, then $x\\mapsto x-4$: dilate horizontally by a factor of $2$, then translate right by $4$ units.\n\nThe new coordinate is\n$$\\begin{align*}x'&=2(8)+4\\\\x'&=20.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q17-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=f\\left(\\frac{x-2}{2}\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$18$",
          "worked": "Replace $x\\mapsto\\frac{x}{2}$, then $x\\mapsto x-2$: dilate horizontally by a factor of $2$, then translate right by $2$ units.\n\n$$y=f\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)\\quad\\text{then}\\quad y=f\\left(\\frac{x-2}{2}\\right).$$\n\nThe new coordinate is\n$$\\begin{align*}x'&=2(8)+2\\\\x'&=18.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q17-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=f\\left(\\frac{x}{3}+1\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$21$",
          "worked": "Write $y=f\\left(\\frac{x+3}{3}\\right)$. Replace $x\\mapsto\\frac{x}{3}$, then $x\\mapsto x+3$: dilate horizontally by a factor of $3$, then translate left by $3$ units.\n\nThe new coordinate is\n$$\\begin{align*}x'&=3(8)-3\\\\x'&=21.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q17-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$y=f\\left(\\frac{x+1}{3}\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$23$",
          "worked": "Replace $x\\mapsto\\frac{x}{3}$, then $x\\mapsto x+1$: dilate horizontally by a factor of $3$, then translate left by $1$ unit.\n\n$$y=f\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)\\quad\\text{then}\\quad y=f\\left(\\frac{x+1}{3}\\right).$$\n\nThe new coordinate is\n$$\\begin{align*}x'&=3(8)-1\\\\x'&=23.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      }
    ]
